{"parentUuid":"a03f999f-e37c-499f-b6d2-13ea61232950","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a3bef849bbe8777ab","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_014zAe7VChnMaNqb6W6V9zKe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KP6efg23YonqJ99jHgvpou","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/simpl_bool_fix/api/tools/explain.html","prompt":"Extract all functions in cpmpy.tools.explain: signatures, default solvers, time complexity hints, and any benchmark comments. Focus on mus, quickxplain, optimal_mus, marco, mcs/mss enumerators. Include the exact import path."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4290,"cache_read_input_tokens":34437,"output_tokens":327,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4290},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":327,"cache_read_input_tokens":34437,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4290,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4290,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caot3eJXCxNFa1m6gnNtB","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"d4c72cc2-4945-4e46-a81f-ac3c2225b2c0","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:59:54.750Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a03f999f-e37c-499f-b6d2-13ea61232950","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a3bef849bbe8777ab","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018yNFu12XBKWPjyoxLsiAAM","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"group MUS\" \"high level\" constraint level CP MILP enumeration algorithm\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Constraints DOI 10.1007/s10601-015-9183-0 Fast, Flexible MUS Enumeration\",\"url\":\"https://sun.iwu.edu/~mliffito/publications/constraints_liffiton_marco.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Debugging Unsatisfiable Constraint Models - CP 2016\",\"url\":\"http://cp2016.a4cp.org/program/workshops/ws-modref-papers/Leo.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Exploiting Symmetries in MUS Computation\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2412.13606\"},{\"title\":\"Fast, flexible MUS enumeration | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/276905908_Fast_flexible_MUS_enumeration\"},{\"title\":\"Parallelizing Partial MUS Enumeration Wenting Zhao and Mark H. Lifﬁton\",\"url\":\"https://sun.iwu.edu/~mliffito/publications/ictai16_zhao_liffiton_MARCOs.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Exact Solution Techniques for Two-dimensional Cutting and Packing\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/am/pii/S0377221720306111\"},{\"title\":\"A Comprehensive Guide to Modeling Techniques in Mixed-Integer Linear Programming | by Bruno Scalia C. F. Leite | TDS Archive | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/data-science/a-comprehensive-guide-to-modeling-techniques-in-mixed-integer-linear-programming-3e96cc1bc03d\"},{\"title\":\"Constraint Generation Algorithm for the Minimum Connectivity Inference Problem\",\"url\":\"https://export.arxiv.org/pdf/1908.09586\"},{\"title\":\"Mixed-Integer Linear Programming (MILP) Algorithms - MATLAB & Simulink\",\"url\":\"https://www.mathworks.com/help/optim/ug/mixed-integer-linear-programming-algorithms.html\"},{\"title\":\"Fast, flexible MUS enumeration | Constraints | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10601-015-9183-0\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found several relevant research papers and resources related to MUS (Minimal Unsatisfiable Subsets) enumeration algorithms, particularly as they apply to constraint programming and high-level constraint models.\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n### High-Level Constraint Models and MUS Enumeration\n\nCurrent MUS enumeration algorithms are usually not aimed at high-level, structured constraint models, and tend to not scale well for them. However, a MUS detection algorithm can take advantage of high-level model structure as an approach to improve performance.\n\n### MARCO Algorithm\n\nThe MARCO algorithm for MUS enumeration analyzes an infeasible constraint system by exploring its power set and uses a Boolean formula to keep track of the subsets whose satisfiability has been determined to reduce the future search space.\n\n### Multi-Level/Constraint-Level Enumeration\n\nThe deepening approach can discover MUSes at the level of individual program level constraints much faster than the full enumeration approach, which relates to working at different constraint levels. If the enumeration algorithm is configured to find MUSes at greater depths, the diagnoses will involve constraints introduced by decompositions of the model-level constraints.\n\n### Integration with CP/MILP\n\nThe search results reference work on debugging unsatisfiable constraint models in CP (Constraint Programming) contexts and discuss how MUS enumeration can be applied to different paradigms, including constraints with Boolean variables that can be generalized to richer constraint-solving paradigms such as SMT, MIP, or CP.\n\nThese resources suggest an active research area in adapting MUS enumeration algorithms to work effectively with high-level, structured constraint models at different abstraction levels.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"6b497564-3ad2-406f-8a6c-e6ad91797eff","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:59:59.433Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a03f999f-e37c-499f-b6d2-13ea61232950","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d4c72cc2-4945-4e46-a81f-ac3c2225b2c0","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a3bef849bbe8777ab","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KP6efg23YonqJ99jHgvpou","type":"tool_result","content":"# CPMpy Explanation Tools Functions\n\n## Import Path\n`cpmpy.tools.explain`\n\n## Core Functions\n\n### MUS (Minimal Unsatisfiable Subset)\n\n**`cpmpy.tools.explain.mus.mus(soft, hard=[], solver='ortools')`**\n- Deletion-based algorithm using assumption variables and unsat core extraction\n- Requires solver support for `assumptions` parameter and `get_core()`\n- Compatible solvers: ortools, exact, z3, pysat\n- Time complexity: Iteratively shrinks unsat cores\n\n**`cpmpy.tools.explain.mus.quickxplain(soft, hard=[], solver='ortools')`**\n- Finds preferred minimal unsatisfiable subset based on constraint ordering\n- Lower-indexed constraints preferred over higher-indexed ones\n- Requires assumption support and unsat core extraction\n- Based on Junker (2004) algorithm\n\n**`cpmpy.tools.explain.mus.optimal_mus(soft, hard=[], weights=None, solver='ortools', hs_solver='ortools', do_solution_hint=True)`**\n- Discovers optimal MUS per linear objective function\n- Default behavior: returns smallest MUS\n- Uses iterative correction subset generation and hitting set computation\n- Recommendation: Use incremental solver (e.g., Gurobi) for hitting set computation\n- Implementation based on OCUS algorithm (Gamba et al., 2023)\n\n### MSS (Maximal Satisfiable Subset)\n\n**`cpmpy.tools.explain.mss.mss(soft, hard=[], solver='ortools')`**\n- Computes subset maximizing total constraint count\n\n**`cpmpy.tools.explain.mss.mss_grow(soft, hard=[], solver='ortools')`**\n- Greedy addition approach via assumption-based solving\n- Exploits solutions to add multiple constraints simultaneously\n- Incremental solver recommended; no optimality guarantee\n\n**`cpmpy.tools.explain.mss.mss_opt(soft, hard=[], weights=1, solver='ortools')`**\n- Weighted variant maximizing sum of constraint weights\n\n### MCS (Minimal Correction Subset)\n\n**`cpmpy.tools.explain.mcs.mcs(soft, hard=[], solver='ortools')`**\n- Removes minimal constraint subset to achieve satisfiability\n- Requires optimization support\n\n**`cpmpy.tools.explain.mcs.mcs_grow(soft, hard, solver='ortools')`**\n- Greedy removal via assumptions; incremental solvers advised\n- No optimality guarantee\n\n**`cpmpy.tools.explain.mcs.mcs_opt(soft, hard, weights=1, solver='ortools')`**\n- Weighted variant minimizing sum of removal weights\n\n### MARCO (MUS/MCS Enumeration)\n\n**`cpmpy.tools.explain.marco.marco(soft, hard=[], solver='ortools', map_solver='ortools', return_mus=True, return_mcs=True, do_solution_hint=True)`**\n- Enumerates both MUSes and MCSes iteratively\n- Grows SAT seeds to MSS; shrinks UNSAT seeds to MUS\n- Map solver constraints prevent MUS supersets\n- Based on Liffiton et al. (2016)\n- Recommendation: Use incremental map solver (Gurobi, pysat, exact)\n\n### Utilities\n\n**`cpmpy.tools.explain.utils.make_assump_model(soft, hard=[], name=None)`**\n- Constructs implied versions of soft constraints for core extraction"}]},"uuid":"817d87cc-a7c3-450d-9932-6536d919726c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:03.266Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d4c72cc2-4945-4e46-a81f-ac3c2225b2c0","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"817d87cc-a7c3-450d-9932-6536d919726c","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a3bef849bbe8777ab","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01HjFHDcPHAibNtQjeXThvhz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent. I have comprehensive material. Let me write the report now.\n\n---\n\n# MUS 提取算法深度调研：Benders 子问题 nogood 注入\n\n## 一、主要算法横向对比\n\n| 算法 | 时间复杂度 (T_solve = 一次 SAT/CP 求解) | 实现库 | 适用场景 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Naive Deletion** (Bakker 1993) | O(\\|S\\|·T_solve)，每次 reset | `cpmpy.tools.explain.mus_naive` | 求解器不支持 assumption 的退路，\"terribly slow\" |\n| **Assumption Deletion** | O(\\|S\\|·T_solve_inc)，T_solve_inc 通常远 < T_solve | `pysat.examples.musx`、`cpmpy.tools.explain.mus`、`get_core()` | 默认首选，简单稳健 |\n| **QuickXplain** (Junker 2004) | O(k·log(\\|S\\|/k)·T_solve)，k = MUS 大小；常数比 deletion 略高 | `cpmpy.tools.explain.quickxplain` | k << \\|S\\| 时显著更快；带优先序的 MUS |\n| **Insertion-based** | O(\\|S\\|·k·T_solve) | 自实现 | 几乎不用；只在需要\"全部 MUS\"时和 MARCO 配合 |\n| **OCUS / Optimal MUS** | 多次 hitting set + SAT 调用 | `cpmpy.tools.explain.optimal_mus` (Gamba 2023) | 需要\"最小\"或\"加权最小\"MUS；贵 |\n| **MARCO** (Liffiton 2016) | 在线枚举多个 MUS / MCS | `cpmpy.tools.explain.marco` | 需要多个 MUS 增加 nogood 信息量 |\n| **ReMUS / UNIMUS / GRAPE-MUST** | 2024 改进，基于递归分区/图剪枝 | 学术原型，无 Python 包装 | 大规模枚举，超出我们需要 |\n| **CP-SAT 原生 `SufficientAssumptionsForInfeasibility`** | 单次求解内部 heuristic 缩减 | OR-Tools | 启发式、非 minimal、单线程 + 无目标才工作 |\n\n## 二、关键事实（直接影响我们设计）\n\n1. **OR-Tools 的核不是 minimal**：官方明确说 `SufficientAssumptionsForInfeasibility()` 是启发式、不保证最小，且和目标函数、多 worker 不兼容。要真正 minimal 必须外层做 deletion / QX。\n2. **CPMpy 的 OR-Tools 后端是 stateless 的**：`CPM_ortools` 每次 `solve(assumptions=…)` 都从头开始，没有 incremental 学习子句保留——这是 Python 接口的设计缺陷，不是算法问题。Lagniez-Biere SAT'13 显示真正的 incremental（保留 learned clauses）能给 deletion-MUS 带来数量级加速，但 CP-SAT Python 接口拿不到。\n3. **CPMpy 已经把脏活做完了**：`cpmpy.tools.explain` 模块包含 `mus`, `quickxplain`, `optimal_mus`, `mcs`, `marco`，全都接 OR-Tools 后端、API 一致。我们不需要重写 QuickXplain 或 deletion。\n4. **Constraint-level (group) MUS** 正是 CPMpy 默认行为：`make_assump_model()` 给每条 soft constraint 配一个 selector boolean，`get_core()` 返回的就是 constraint 粒度的核。\n\n## 三、与 OR-Tools CP-SAT 的对接方式（三层）\n\n**Layer A — 直接 OR-Tools 原生**：\n```python\nb = model.NewBoolVar(f\"sel_{i}\")\nmodel.Add(constraint).OnlyEnforceIf(b)\nsolver.Solve(model)              # 解前 model.AddAssumption(b) 或 add_assumptions([...])\nsolver.SufficientAssumptionsForInfeasibility()  # 返回 proto index 列表，非 minimal\n```\n缺点：不 minimal、不能配目标。\n\n**Layer B — CPMpy 包装**（推荐落地点）：\n```python\nfrom cpmpy.tools.explain import mus, quickxplain\ncore = mus(soft=soft_constraints, hard=hard_constraints, solver=\"ortools\")\n```\n内部就是 deletion + `get_core()`，每轮重建 OR-Tools 模型；调用复杂度 O(\\|S\\|·T_solve)，T_solve 是单次 CP-SAT 求解。\n\n**Layer C — 自己用 PySAT** 走 SAT 层：只有当我们能把 binding 子问题完全 CNF 化才划算，对我们 routing/flow 子问题不适用——CP 结构丢了反而更慢。**结论：不走 PySAT。**\n\n## 四、为各 Benders 子问题选算法\n\n| 子问题 | 失败结构 | 推荐 | 理由 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `binding_subproblem` | 端口绑定不可行，soft 约束 ≈ O(端口数) ~ 数十到几百 | **QuickXplain** via `cpmpy.tools.explain.quickxplain` | k 通常 << \\|S\\|，分治赢；带绑定优先序天然贴 QX |\n| `routing_subproblem` | 网格路径不可行，soft = 路由要求 | **Assumption Deletion** via `cpmpy.tools.explain.mus` | k 与 \\|S\\| 比较接近，deletion 常数小 |\n| `flow_subproblem` | 多商品流诊断 | **Deletion**，只对失败商品集合做；用 CPMpy 的 `mus` | 同上，规模小 |\n\n**额外建议**：每 5–10 轮 Benders 在最关键的失败上跑一次 MARCO 取 2–3 个 MUS，灌多条 nogood，比每轮单 MUS 信息量大；MARCO 调用也是一行 `cpmpy.tools.explain.marco.marco(...)`。\n\n## 五、价格（必须知道的成本）\n\n- 单次 QuickXplain ≈ `log(|S|) × T_solve` 量级；deletion ≈ `|S| × T_solve`。子问题 \\|S\\|≈100、T_solve≈50ms 时，QX 大约 0.3–0.7s/次，deletion 大约 5s/次。\n- CPMpy 因为 stateless，T_solve 含完整 presolve 重启——大约比理论 incremental 慢 2–5 倍。这是为了用 Python 必须付的税。\n- **不是每个失败都值得提 MUS**：建议只在 master 反复命中同一类失败（≥2 次）时触发 MUS 提取，否则灌一条粗 nogood（整个 master 决策的否定）就够。\n- **异步可行**：把 MUS 提取放后台 worker，主循环继续探下一候选；MUS 准备好再注入 master。CPMpy 调用是普通函数，扔 `concurrent.futures` 即可。\n\n## 六、我们项目的具体技术方案 + 工程量\n\n**方案**：在 `src/search/benders_loop.py` 失败分支后加一个 `mus_extractor` 模块：\n\n```\nsrc/search/mus_extractor.py     # 新文件，~200 行\n  - extract_mus(subproblem_kind, soft, hard) -> List[int]\n  - 内部按 kind 路由到 cpmpy.tools.explain.{mus, quickxplain}\n  - 失败时退回 OR-Tools SufficientAssumptionsForInfeasibility 作 best-effort\nsrc/models/binding_subproblem.py  # 改：暴露 soft/hard constraint 列表（不直接 build CP-SAT model）\nsrc/models/routing_subproblem.py  # 同上\nsrc/models/flow_subproblem.py     # 同上\nsrc/search/benders_loop.py        # 改：失败 ≥2 次时调 mus_extractor，把核翻成 nogood 加到 master\nsrc/tests/test_mus_extractor.py   # 新文件，构造 3 种已知 UNSAT 子问题验证\n```\n\n**依赖新增**：`cpmpy>=0.9.24`（MIT）。已经依赖 ortools，无版本冲突。\n\n**工程量估计**：\n- 暴露 soft/hard 接口（3 个子问题模型）：~1 天\n- `mus_extractor.py` + 算法路由 + 异步包装：~1 天\n- nogood 翻译回 master（核 → master 决策的子集禁止）：~1 天，是最 tricky 的——因为 binding/routing/flow 的 selector 要映射回 master 的 placement 变量\n- 测试 + 性能基准：~1 天\n\n**预期收益**：Round 3 调研里方案 C 估计加速 2–5×，前提是 nogood 比\"整个 master 决策\"更精确——MUS 让这个前提成立。如果 MUS 提取本身吃掉 30% 时间但 master 收敛轮数减半，净收益依然显著正向。\n\n**风险点**：CPMpy stateless 让 MUS 提取成本被低估；建议在 S6 worker matrix 里加一个 `mus_overhead_ratio` 监控指标，超过 0.5 就降级到 best-effort 模式。\n\n---\n\nSources:\n- [CPMpy unsat core extraction docs](https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/latest/unsat_core_extraction.html)\n- [CPMpy explain tools API](https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/simpl_bool_fix/api/tools/explain.html)\n- [PySAT MUSX docs](https://pysathq.github.io/docs/html/api/examples/musx.html)\n- [Junker 2004 QuickXplain (formal proof)](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10462-022-10149-w)\n- [Lagniez-Biere SAT'13 incremental MUS](https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/LagniezBiere-SAT13.pdf)\n- [Liffiton et al. MARCO fast flexible enumeration](https://sun.iwu.edu/~mliffito/publications/constraints_liffiton_marco.pdf)\n- [OR-Tools assumptions discussion](https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/qlVv2uSq1uo)\n- [CP-SAT Primer parameters](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html)\n- [Codato-Fischetti Combinatorial Benders Cuts](https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-540-25960-2_14)\n- [GRAPE-MUST 2024](https://proceedings.mlr.press/v238/lymperopoulos24a/lymperopoulos24a.pdf)\n- [MUST tool 2020](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7439739/)\n- [CPMpy MUS source](https://github.com/CPMpy/cpmpy/blob/master/cpmpy/tools/explain/mus.py)"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3046,"cache_read_input_tokens":38727,"output_tokens":3913,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3046},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":3913,"cache_read_input_tokens":38727,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3046,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3046,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caot4orXEh4yCey9GR83W","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"60b330f7-1d75-4983-b4bf-0caf7ac685d5","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:01:10.558Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
